script = ExtResource("1_g070l")
entry_name = "Function"
description = "In Python a function is a reusable block of code that only runs when you call it. We define a function with the def keyword, give it a name, and add parentheses after the name.

Here is a sample code using a function:

def my_function():
    print(\"Hello from a function\")

my_function()

The line def my_function(): defines the function, and the indented line under it is the body that runs when the function is called. Nothing happens until we call it with my_function().

A function can also take values called parameters, and it can send a value back to the caller with the return keyword. For example:

def greet(name):
    return \"Hello \" + name

print(greet(\"World\"))

Here the function greet takes a name, returns a greeting string, and print shows the result Hello World."
keyword = "def"
language = "python"
category = "Hard"
